# Keep the build context to what the image actually needs.
#
# The Dockerfile ends in `COPY . .`, so without this file every one of these
# lands in a layer of a published image. `.git/` is the one that matters: it is
# the repository's entire history, it is useless at runtime, and Milestone 5 is
# the point where these images stop being local and start being pushed to ECR.
#
# `tests/` and `pytest.ini` are DELIBERATELY NOT excluded. Milestone 6 gives
# every service repo a workflow that lints and tests on pull requests, and if
# that is ever done in a container stage rather than on the runner, the tests
# have to be reachable from the build context. Excluding them would make a test
# stage impossible rather than merely unused, which is a bigger loss than the
# few KB they cost.

.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
README.md

# Python build artefacts. These are host-built, and on a different interpreter
# or architecture than the image's - copying them in is worse than useless.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Virtualenvs. `pip install` already ran against requirements.txt inside the
# image; a host venv would shadow it with the wrong platform's binaries.
.venv/
venv/

# No service repo has a .env today. That is exactly why it is listed: this
# costs nothing now and stops a developer's local credentials being baked into
# a published image later. .env.example is intentionally NOT excluded - it
# carries no secrets and documents the required variables.
.env
